Mike Fournier, cunningly disguised as fournim@sympatico.ca wrote:

> 1) If you have a bag in your inventory, is the only way to put
> something in it, is by dropping it, then useing the "loot" command and
> then choose to put something in it?  Is there an easier way.

A bag is a tool. To use a tool, use the 'a'pply command.

> 2) I don't have one, but if/when I get a bag of Holding. Is it
> unlimited? Would that be the only bag I would ever need , and no longer
> need bags after that?

A blessed bag of holding reduces the weight of the stuff inside by 75%.
So, no, you still cannot carry an unlimited weight, but you can carry four
times your normal carrying capacity.

> 3) I have been reading various online guides on Nethack. One thing I see
> that is mentioned often, is people seem to hold in high priority to
> wish for a Scroll of Charging, or a Magic Marker to create scrolls of
> charging.  What is the importance of the Scroll of Charging? I imagine
> it is used to recharge a wand or something or other. What item do you
> then deem so important to recharge so often?

You can recharge a wand of wishing (once). So when you use a wand of
wishing, you should first wish for two blessed scrolls of recharging. This
way, if the wand had only one charge, you can read the scroll of charging
and get it back up to three charges.

